Looking at the dependencies, T3 depends only on T1, while T2 needs to handle the `kind=review` routing and create the dispatch-review-result handler. T3's subtask says to wire the reviewer briefing into "the reviewer dispatch path added in T2", which means T2 should have already set up that infrastructure. Since T2 hasn't been completed yet, I need to figure out what T3 can reasonably implement without those pieces in place.

The core of T3 is creating the briefing generator and the review-pr skill, along with dispatch-reviewer.ts that ties them together. The wiring itself is mostly done within T3's own files. T2 will handle the broader plumbing like ABI types, reap-loop routing, and the dispatch-review-result handler.

